WEBVTT

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.440
This special underground theater
show here in Bangkok, Thailand,

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.610
that we have been bringing
to you ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.770
is finally drawing to a close.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:27.830
Finally, tonight, in the year 2619,
the strongest man on land...

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.440
oh, I beg your pardon.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.500
The strongest man <i>underground</i>
shall be decided.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.110
So they actually do things like this.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.740
I've seen it a hundred times in manga.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.120
It might happen a lot in manga, but...

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.180
In reality, there are company
presidents and oil tycoons

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:56.600
that make millions and billions in a month.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.550
The people here

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.230
are that kind of out-of-this-world rich.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.620
When people like that get together,

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.700
it might still be impossible to stop time,

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:12.970
but putting on a show where people
kill each other is easy, huh...

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.320
So they're not dead yet?

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:18.830
Yeah.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.210
First, in the blue corner, is this man!

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:36.410
The supernova twenty-something
with a bit of a shady past.

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:38.990
Hi-za-ma-ru!

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.750
Hizamaru Akari!

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.470
He's 177cm tall and weighs 91 kilograms!

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:50.130
Citizenship is Japan, and the martial
art he practices is karate.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:54.940
So that's him...

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.930
<b><i>Mutation</i></b>

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:30.520
His childhood sweetheart,
who grew up with him in the orphanage,

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:35.780
is plagued with some unknown
illness and suffering!

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.940
<i>Does he have to say this every time?</i>

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.970
The only cure is to have
an organ transplant.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:48.840
Hizamaru-kun wants the prize money
for her sake, no matter what!

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:49.830
Yeah!

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:53.470
That's right! You got
that, you rich bastards?!

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:56.480
Well done... and for some bitch
you haven't even screwed.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:01.490
But his opponent in the final
round is a strong one.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.630
The undefeated king since
this tournament started...

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.480
Brian Chaomy-kun, age 14!

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.000
He stands 251cm tall and
weighs in at 342 kilograms!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.750
His citizenship is American, and he doesn't
practice any form of martial arts.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.190
He is a natural-born fighter.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.140
What the hell is this?!

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.510
Brian-kun here would
usually be omnivorous,

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:41.940
but he's only been fed human
flesh for quite a long time.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.360
<i>So you guys</i>

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:46.870
<i>never had any intention of letting me win.</i>

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.280
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:59.510
Yuriko! I'm coming to save you now!

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.520
Hey, audience!

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.620
Get riled up!

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:15.310
I'm going to shatter this
absurd, scripted scenario!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.650
<i>The likelihood of this
succeeding is slim, but...</i>

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.600
You know, too,

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.620
right?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.420
Go home!

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:19.250
Is watching me waste away that

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.960
amusing?!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.880
Coming to visit me day after day?!

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.330
You...

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.950
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.970
You're just a monster!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.510
Just go home!

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.230
This isn't normal.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:44.000
We came here to see this?

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.830
If everything we researched is correct,

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.240
the one who isn't normal
is actually Hizamaru Akari.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.370
Ah, Akari-kun...

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.940
I said something really terrible last week.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.260
Well, maybe it was perfect timing.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.090
Eh?

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.380
If I keep holding onto something so childish,

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.550
I won't be able to keep up with the fashion
of the other college students.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:16.890
We found one.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:19.270
We found a possible donor.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.400
You're kidding...

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.390
It's the truth. It's at a
hospital in another country.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.470
Now picture it, Yuriko. You're almost there.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.430
What do you want to do as
soon as you're better?

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.430
I want to eat ramen.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:41.710
Got it. Let's do it.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.090
I want to go snowboarding.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.420
Yeah, I can't wait until winter.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.610
I want to try alcohol.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.570
Sure, just don't drink too much.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:51.400
I want to go to Space Land.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:54.160
Yeah, I'm sure it's not
too crowded right now.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:57.850
And... and... and...

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:11.320
Why? Why are you so nice, Akari-kun?

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.070
Of course I am.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:20.780
I... You're the one who gave me my kindness.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.890
Ever since that day.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.010
I lo—

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.770
You're very precious to me.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.420
<i>Because you're my friend.</i>

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.970
Huh? He got up...

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:10.170
An old-fashioned knock out!

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.550
But what's this?

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:23.030
Wh-What...

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.520
Could this be...?

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.300
I can't believe it...

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.990
H-Hizamaru Akari...

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:37.730
turned it around and won!

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:40.080
So there was one more.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.180
A child that was born after the surgery...

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.040
What?!

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:48.960
You promised! It was a promise!

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:51.170
S-Stop...

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:53.970
Operate on Yuriko!

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:59.980
W-We sold the girl...

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.020
Wha— To who?!

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.350
You bastard...

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:16.740
Bring Yuriko back right n—

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:17.990
She died.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.050
We did what we could,

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:22.110
but the day before yesterday...

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:33.260
Don't.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:36.280
Lie. To me!

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.860
These people never intended
to find a donor for you.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:47.060
They're just assholes.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:49.560
By the time we found out about her existence

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:54.110
and went to get her,
it was already too late.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:56.070
I'm sorry we didn't make it in time.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.570
What... the hell...

00:09:58.610 --> 00:09:59.710
Give her back.

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:01.760
Give her back...

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:05.200
Give...

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.530
Give her back!

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.010
Akari-kun.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:25.780
Would you like to save children
that have the same disease as her?

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.110
Sorry for the late introductions.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.770
I'm the commanding officer

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:41.120
of the United Nations Aeronautics and Space Administration
U-NASA's Mars Exploration Team, Komachi Shokichi.

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:44.840
Likewise, I'm the second in
command, Michelle K. Davis.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:46.660
U-NASA?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:47.500
That's right.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.750
The disease that stole the
life of your childhood friend

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.800
is no ordinary infectious disease.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:55.290
It's a virus that came
from outside the Earth.

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:02.720
The virus will continue to spread,
and many people will die.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:07.520
In order to stop that, in two years

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.000
we will fly to Mars.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:10.520
Mars?

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.990
We need you. We need your strength,

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.530
and that raw rage you have inside you.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:22.410
My friend died on Mars.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:30.700
Anyone else could only comfort you
for the pain you're feeling.

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:37.230
However, people like us, who have
the same piercing rage boiling inside us...

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.840
We have been bound by a fate
stronger than blood,

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:44.480
and become a swarm.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:48.690
Let's go.

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:58.850
I loved you,

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.010
Yuri-chan.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.740
I really did.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:05.100
I...

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:06.830
I...

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:11.050
Man... I wonder why...

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:13.710
I'm so mad at everything.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:22.430
Sorry, Michelle-chan. You had
some spare sunglasses, right?

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:23.720
Can I borrow them?

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:25.890
Come on, hurry!

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:30.570
I'm sorry I wasn't thinking and put
-chan at the end of your name!

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.400
I don't care.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:40.680
You can call me that.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:12:59.930
Looks like you've finally woken up.

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.140
Ah.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.510
U-Um... Michelle-chan?

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:07.260
Don't mess with me. You're younger than me.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.580
S-Sorry.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:14.310
If you're going to insist on calling me that,
you're going to have to become my husband first.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.410
Thanks.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:22.600
Since it's already noon,
I must have been asleep a full day.

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:24.490
No, it was a week.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:25.240
Eh?

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:26.860
You're kidding!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.520
Why would I lie?

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:30.320
There's a tube attached
to your dick, isn't there?

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:31.070
Eh?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:32.660
Uh...!

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.880
I'm the one who attached it.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:38.460
I'm kidding, you idiot.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.920
It just means the surgery
you had was that rough.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.130
It's to force

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:47.540
the human body to be strong enough
to survive in Mars' atmosphere.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:53.930
We knew that your surgery
would be a success, though.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:14:00.360
You already had most of what the surgery
would usually involve from your parent.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.150
Just like I did.

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:09.240
Then... what's the success rate
for a normal human being?

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:11.300
Thirty...

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:12.580
...six percent?

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:16.640
Yeah. It's definitely not
a high survival rate.

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.990
It's not 3.6%?

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.530
Then that's pretty high.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.110
No. Over half of them die.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.860
Those are better odds than us going back home to

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:27.820
become civil servants and get a pension

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:29.550
without being killed in the line of duty.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:33.000
You really lack alertness, don't you?

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.350
But you agree, don't you, Sheila?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:42.040
Well, I guess there's a much higher
chance than living in Grande Mexico.

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:46.610
But why do we need to modify
our bodies to go to Mars?

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:51.620
If the air is just thin up there,
we have masks and space suits.

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:54.810
We will eventually be explaining that.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.450
Adolf.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.410
Captain Komachi.

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:04.140
There you are.

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:05.740
You were here?

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:07.090
Who's that?

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:12.260
This is a reservist who will
be undergoing the surgery.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:15.000
I'm Eva Frost.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:18.230
Oh, so she's in the
same boat as these guys.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:18.870
I'm Sheila Levitt.

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:20.230
I'm Marcos.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:20.350
Nice to—

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:21.590
I'm Alex!

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:22.730
Hey!

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.040
You guys...

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:25.820
Hey, now.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.470
This is Adolf.

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:31.300
He's an executive staff member
from the Germany division.

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:33.290
He's going to be your superior.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:36.240
Oh, you didn't have to introduce me.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.280
I have no intention of remembering them.

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.440
What did you say?!

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:43.010
So, you are the last four
to undergo the surgery...

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:47.630
Considering the probabilities,
one or two of you will die.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:52.180
Well, pray that it happens
while you're still under.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.980
Do you think we're just
going to shut up and ta—

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:56.290
Hey, you should watch how you say—

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.270
I'm only speaking the truth.

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:01.370
Captain, I'll leave "that" to you.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.420
Are you all right? Here.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:12.060
Uh, no, I can get up myself.

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:17.020
<i>Well... Whatever.</i>

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:22.040
Let's go, Akari. Also...

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:25.890
I'll let you go this time,

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:28.540
but if you happen to slip during
training or on a mission

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:32.050
and look anywhere below my
glasses, I will not forgive you.

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:38.560
Right.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:41.310
Why aren't you all scared?

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:46.000
I mean, 60% die...

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:51.810
Not only does she look a bit unfortunate,
but she's super negative.

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:53.920
Yeah, she's negative boobies.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.530
Oh?

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:58.950
Take a look, Eva-chan.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:01.280
There appears to be a reservist that has

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:03.460
gone through the procedure
walking over there.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.230
And they're totally fine.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.690
This is what 40% looks like!

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:10.930
The surgery was no biggie, was it?

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:12.720
Eh? Yeah...

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:15.000
But my chances of the procedure

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.470
succeeding were higher because of my genetics...

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.690
Oh, here we go. So you're that kind of guy.

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:26.480
What? You're trying to appeal that
you're different from others?

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.800
I was hoping you'd be able to
read your surroundings more.

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.350
Can I hit them?

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:31.940
Sure, just don't push yourself.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.590
Hey, hey, hey...

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:34.860
What's the matter, Marcos-kun?

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.820
I'm sorry, they're idiots.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.520
They've been like this since we were kids.

00:17:39.520 --> 00:17:41.390
I-It's okay.

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:44.620
I'm envious that you know others.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.880
I'm... alone, so...

00:17:59.650 --> 00:17:59.660
Now you can't lay a finger on us!

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.240
You're not alone anymore, Eva-san.

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:02.640
Y-You guys...

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.010
Hey! That's not fair!

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:05.310
Here, let me help.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.800
Let's go for a walk, a walk.

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:07.880
You don't have to add -san
to my name. Eva's fine.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:09.430
S-Stop... Michelle-san!

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.490
Oh, okay.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:23.410
We did things a bit backwards
in Akari's case,

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:27.240
but for the rest of you I'll be explaining
the mission before your surgeries.

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:36.790
This is the alien virus, otherwise
known as the AE virus.

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:38.790
This came from Mars?

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:39.860
That's right.

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.550
Currently, the mortality rate for those

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.640
who have been infected with it has been 100%.

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:48.890
However, the virus samples we currently
find on Earth cannot be cultivated.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:52.130
So we will go to Mars ourselves,

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:57.030
investigate Mars' air,
sand, water, and moss,

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.610
study their existence and variations,

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.410
and bring them back if necessary.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:02.910
That is our mission.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.930
If we are successful, we will be
able to eradicate the virus

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:09.420
and save humanity from extinction.

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:11.410
But there is one problem.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:16.290
All of the unmanned vessels we've sent
for samples have failed to come back.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.290
That is because...

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:22.940
a certain organism always gets in the way.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:31.100
This is Mars' giant cockroach,
the terraformar.

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:35.610
They have evolved to adapt
in Mars' harsh environment

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.950
over the last five hundred years.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:42.050
Forty-two years ago the six
crew members of Bugs 1,

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:46.610
and twenty years ago the thirteen members
of the Bugs 2, were killed by them.

00:19:47.590 --> 00:19:51.920
You mean, these giant
cockroaches... eat people?

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:58.420
If you found a cockroach in your kitchen,
would you pick it up and eat it?

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.260
No, you wouldn't.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:01.930
But you'd kill it.

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:07.210
If you think about it calmly,
you probably don't know why you'd kill it.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:10.140
But you'd kill it with
everything you've got, right?

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:11.900
That's how it is.

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:18.610
This is

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:23.030
the war between humans and cockroaches over
who will continue to exist as a species.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:26.080
The ones who lose...

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:28.180
are the vermin.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:35.580
Christian Era 2620 March 4th

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.220
100 Members

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.900
The Large-Scale Spaceship Annex 1

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:08.910
Will Leave Earth

00:23:00.070 --> 00:23:01.070
Mars.

00:23:01.590 --> 00:23:03.800
The fourth planet of the Solar System.

00:23:03.800 --> 00:23:07.260
The original average temperature is -53 degrees

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:10.030
and the atmospheric pressure is 0.06.

00:23:10.890 --> 00:23:14.850
In order to make this frigid planet an
environment where humans could live,

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:17.810
in the 21st century two kinds of life forms

00:23:17.810 --> 00:23:20.620
were sent to the planet ahead of the humans.

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:23.000
First, a special kind of algae,

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:28.630
and second, an insect with
a powerful ability to breed.

00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:40.110
The cockroach.
